`yo_safe.txt` is `dictionary/safe.txt` from eyo-kernel 4.1.3
(https://github.com/e2yo/eyo-kernel), file SHA-256
11fc6d9c3cc6d0fff6a21cd642fa6aecbf3f9eb784f84ccd78141f32e51e0693
(864903 bytes). It restores the Russian letter yo only where the word
is unambiguous. Voxprint ships this file and reimplements the lookup in
`core/yo.py`. It does not ship the TypeScript library, and it does not
ship `not_safe.txt` (ambiguous homographs such as все / всё).

The eyo-kernel README says the dictionary was first taken from
https://github.com/rin-nas/php-yoficator (that repository publishes no
licence file) and is maintained and distributed by eyo-kernel under the
MIT licence below.

